    "verdict": "At the stated parameters (r = 0.01, rho_u = 0.02), Proposition 14 gives a cost fraction of 0.03 and a speedup of 1 / 0.03 = 33.333x, exceeding the paper's printed 26x by +7.333x (+28.21% over printed; printed is 22.0% below the formula). Obtaining exactly 26x requires rho_u + r = 1/26 = 0.038462 (an extra 0.008462 cost fraction): either rho_u = 0.028462 (37/1300) at r = 0.01, or r = 0.018462 (12/650) at rho_u = 0.02. As r increases, speedup declines hyperbolically as 1/(rho_u + r), crossing break-even (1.0x) at r = 1 - rho_u = 0.98, falling to 0.980x when screening equals execution cost (r = 1), and approaching 0 (~ 1/r) as r -> infinity."
